# liblouis: Unified English Braille Code New Zealand English (Grade 2)
#
#-index-name: English, unified, New Zealand, contracted
#-display-name: Unified English contracted braille as used in New Zealand
#+language:en
#+region:*-NZ
#+type:literary
#+contraction:full
#+grade:2
#+system:ueb-nz
#
# This table implements the policy of the Braille Authority of New
# Zealand Aotearoa Trust, that vowel macrons be indicated in braille
# by the single cell prefix dots 4-5-6 (see
# https://www.banzat.org.nz/documents/BANZATPolicy8TranscribingMaoriTextInBraille.docx
# ). Although under this policy this should only apply to words in the
# Māori language, the reality is that many Māori words are commonly
# used in English texts without being marked up as Māori. This table
# is provided so readers reading in the English language can have such
# words presented in braille using dots 4-5-6 to indicate macrons.
